{
  "format": 4,
  "kind": "session",
  "name": "Live records move the checkpoint",
  "description": "Once a room's recovery completes on a connection, each live record delivered for it (a snapshot, a reaction set) moves its checkpoint C to that record's log_id, and a thread's T moves the same way once loadRoom completes on the connection; live records buffered during a recovery count when it completes, as C becomes the greatest of H and their log_ids. A room frame at that head needs no request, and a resume after a loss starts after the last live record, not where the last recovery ended. A room frame whose head is above them reveals records live delivery didn't bring (a server may drop notifications): the room recovers from C + 1 as before. Pages are not clamped. Each variant ends with its own expectation.",
  "references": [
    "PROTOCOL.md#35-messages",
    "PROTOCOL.md#43-history",
    "PROTOCOL.md#47-reactions"
  ],
  "variants": [
